      <h2>Key Takeaways for Your 10-Year Journey</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>NLV is Year 1 starting point:</strong> Not a final status, but the gateway to everything else</li>
        <li><strong>First renewal in Year 1 extends TIE to 2 years:</strong> You're not renewing annually after that</li>
        <li><strong>183-day rule is strict during NLV years 0-5:</strong> Track your days carefully to avoid renewal denial</li>
        <li><strong>Year 5 is the transformation point:</strong> Permanent residency removes income requirement and unlocks work rights</li>
        <li><strong>Permanent residency gives 10-year card:</strong> No more frequent renewals; long-term stability</li>
        <li><strong>Year 5 is when many NLV holders start businesses:</strong> Legal clarity and work rights make entrepreneurship possible</li>
        <li><strong>Year 10 opens citizenship path:</strong> Language exam + civics exam + 10-year residency = Spanish nationality</li>
        <li><strong>Spanish citizenship grants passport and EU rights:</strong> Full freedom within EU, voting rights, no residency requirements</li>
        <li><strong>Dual citizenship is allowed:</strong> Keep your original nationality while gaining Spanish citizenship</li>
